%erg 0.1
Title: Fix corrupted character in embedded AGENTS.md asset
Created: 2026-05-29
Author: Claude

--- log ---
2026-05-29T15:10Z Claude created — UX audit finding F02 (verified); erg init ships corrupted bytes

--- body ---
## Context

The UX audit (0152, PR #174) found that `erg init` unpacks an AGENTS.md
containing a corrupted character. The embedded asset
`src/go/assets/AGENTS.md:28` reads `random jitter �i 500ms` where it should
read `random jitter ≤ 500ms`. Verified with hexdump: the bytes are
`ef bf bd 69` (U+FFFD REPLACEMENT CHARACTER followed by `i`) where a
`≤ ` (U+2264 + space) belongs.

This is a data-quality bug in a shipped asset: every user who runs
`erg init` receives the corrupted text in the first document they read.
The on-disk repo copy (`tickets/AGENTS.md`) is clean — only the embedded
source asset is corrupted, so it travels in every binary.

## Relevant files

- `src/go/assets/AGENTS.md:28` — the corrupted line (the embedded source)
- `src/go/bootstrap_assets.go` — embeds the asset
- `tests/test_init.sh` — init asset tests (add a guard here)

## Actions

1. Replace the corrupted bytes at `src/go/assets/AGENTS.md:28` with the
   intended `≤ ` (U+2264 + space): `random jitter ≤ 500ms`.
2. Rebuild and confirm `erg init` now unpacks clean UTF-8.
3. Rebuild the bootstrap binary (`make update-bootstrap-binary`).

## Test

Add an assertion to `tests/test_init.sh` (or `test_ux.sh`) that the
init-unpacked `AGENTS.md` contains no U+FFFD replacement character:

```sh
if grep -aq "$(printf '\357\277\275')" "$REPO/tickets/AGENTS.md"; then
    fail "init-unpacked AGENTS.md contains U+FFFD replacement character"
else
    pass "init-unpacked AGENTS.md is clean UTF-8"
fi
```

This catches a wrong implementation (corrupted asset re-embedded), not
merely a different one — the negative control is the current corrupted
asset, which the test must flag.

## Verification

- [ ] `src/go/assets/AGENTS.md` is valid UTF-8 with `≤` at line 28
- [ ] `erg init` in a temp dir unpacks AGENTS.md with no U+FFFD bytes
- [ ] New test fails against the pre-fix asset, passes after the fix
- [ ] Bootstrap binary rebuilt

## Invariants

- Do not alter the *content* of AGENTS.md beyond fixing the byte —
  the embedded copy and any on-disk template should stay in sync.
- `make test` stays green.

## Exit criteria

- The embedded asset is clean UTF-8, `erg init` unpacks it intact, and a
  regression test guards against re-introducing a replacement character.
